  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Meta does not rule out that the unmitigated Muse Wonder Full reaches the high risk threshold for Chemical & Biological under the Meta Superintelligence Scaling Framework, so it applies safety post-training and system-level classifiers for that domain.",
      "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "7",
        "quote": "we do not rule out the model reaching this threshold in the Chemical & Biological domain. Because of that, we apply mitigations designed for this domain, including safety post-training and system-level classifiers."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Meta puts the unmitigated model at moderate or lower for Cybersecurity and Loss of Control, and the mitigated model at moderate or lower in all three domains.",
      "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "7",
        "quote": "Our evaluations put the unmitigated model at “moderate or lower” for both Cybersecurity and Loss of Control before applying our mitigations."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The risk assessment uses results from Muse Wonder Full only, and Meta applies it to every model in the family; the card gives no separate safety results for Muse Wonder.",
      "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "7",
        "quote": "Results below are from Muse Wonder Full, our most capable variant, which is why the assessment covers every model in the family."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [ExploitGym](/evals/exploitgym), Muse Wonder Full captured 92 flags, but only 21 used the intended vulnerability; the other 71 came from unintended vulnerabilities.",
      "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "7",
        "quote": "found that 21 of those used the intended vulnerability, while the other 71 were captured through unintended vulnerabilities."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Two [ABC-Bench](/evals/abc-bench) tasks (Fragment Design and Screening Evasion) have no score because the model refused at a high rate; Meta dropped refusals before scoring.",
      "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "9",
        "quote": "** = High rate of refusals due to safety training. Refusals dropped prior to scoring."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cyber jailbreak success rates are low (0.8% to 9.0%), and highest on RedCode (9.0% single turn, 8.0% multi turn) (lower is better).",
      "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "8",
        "quote": "RedCode Single turn 9.0 Multi turn 8.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The card names no external organization that tested the model; Meta says it worked with third parties on licensed benchmarks, ran threat modeling with outside experts, and engaged with government entities.",
      "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "11",
        "quote": "We ran threat modeling with outside experts, and engaged with government entities and other stakeholders whose input informed our evaluations and requirements."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Meta says its runs of competing models are best-effort, and prompts, tools and runtime may not be tuned for them.",
      "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "quote": "Internally generated competitor runs use common settings where practical but remain best-effort"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Meta says the model is not intended for people under 18, and deployers must assess and reduce the risks of such use.",
      "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "11",
        "quote": "The model is not intended to be used by individuals under the age of 18."
      }
    }
  ],
