  "notes": "Source is the 13-page PDF at research.meta.ai; no saved copy, so no pdfPage (page = PDF page; the PDF prints no page numbers). The model card covers Muse Wonder and Muse Wonder Full, but every safety and risk result is for Muse Wonder Full only (meta/muse-wonder-full). PDF page 3 is the main capability table, an image with no text: it holds numbers for Muse Wonder Full, Muse Wonder, Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra and Claude Opus 5.5. It was skipped because its quotes cannot be checked against the text. The ABC-Bench Fragment Design and Screening Evasion rows have no number (refusals) and were skipped. The Meta Superintelligence Scaling Framework (v2.1) was renamed from the Advanced AI Scaling Framework, so frameworks uses meta-aasf. Loss of Control is mapped to ai_rnd_autonomy, as in the Muse Spark 1.1 card. No safety tester is named. Meta says a full safety report will follow (blog post)."
}
